# Plan and addons

The product plan is `PLAN.md` at the repo root. Commit it, and `private/profile.yaml`, only on the local branch `private`. Never commit them on `main`. Never merge `private` into `main`. Never push `private` to the public remote. Do not paste household facts from the plan into code, tests, or the README.

Sections above `## Addons` are the original lock. Open work is an addon that is not marked shipped. Do not treat a shipped addon as a build order.

Anything new — a feature idea, or a change of scope — goes under `## Addons` in `PLAN.md`. Start the item with `Addon:`. Do not build an addon unless the user asks for that addon.

When an addon has shipped, replace its body with one line: `Shipped.` A parked choice may be a second sentence. Do not leave the build instructions. The planner does this when the slice is reported done. Board files stay a status and an inbox. They do not grow a log. A cursor rule is updated in place. A new rule file is only for a new duty.

Do not name another website, calculator, or design shot in code, tests, docs, the README, or a commit message.

The result may show one named year of monthly averages from cashflow after purchase (Kaufen and Mieten columns). No verdict, savings headline, or stay-years slider.

```markdown
### Addon: short name

What to add, and what to leave out.
```

When a change makes this rule stale, update the rule in the same change.
